# All variables here are optional. The site builds and runs without a .env file.

# Enables Plausible analytics. Set to the domain registered in your Plausible
# account, e.g. zaviah.org. When unset, src/components/Analytics.tsx injects
# nothing and no analytics script is loaded. plausible.io is already allowed by
# the Content-Security-Policy in netlify.toml and public/_headers.
# VITE_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=zaviah.org

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form: no variables needed.
#
# It uses Netlify Forms. Netlify detects the form from public/__forms.html during
# the build, and every submission appears under Forms in the Netlify dashboard.
#
# One-time setup, outside this repo: in Netlify, open Forms > Form notifications and add an
# email notification for the "contact" form pointing at the address in src/lib/constants.ts
# (EMAIL). Without that notification, submissions are still stored but nobody is emailed.
